{"note":"ledger listing"},"err":true},{"tool":"brief","args":{},"obs":{"brief":"Dope Fe3InTe2 (C3) with Zn. Above a critical Zn content the structure distorts to a lower symmetry; the device needs that distorted phase. Deliver a single-phase sample of the distorted phase whose magnetic ordering temperature is 263.7 +/- 3.0 K.\nLab rules and conventions:\n- There is no one-step synthesis. Make every sample on the bench: take vessels (jar, boat, ampoule, vial,\n  crucible), weigh element powders, grind, press, load and seal ampoules, heat in a furnace, collect the product.\n- Element powders live in the argon glove box; a vessel is weighed into where it is. Ar sealing needs the glove\n  box; the furnaces (2) are outside it. Chalcogenides must be heated in a sealed ampoule.\n- Reaction needs roughly 650 C + 350 C per unit nominal x. Safety: never set a furnace above 850 C. A second\n  safety violation locks the lab.\n- Measurements cost budget: xrd 1, squid_mt 1, edx 1 (12 in total). Bench work, weighing contents,\n  reference_cif, env_log, ledger and status are free but take simulated time. Time limit: 14 days.\n- Products are named B001, B002, ... when collected. Deliver with deliver(product, evidence=[ledger ids]); the\n  evidence must include an xrd and a squid_mt of that product. Delivering ends the task.\n- Specification: the delivered sample must also contain less than 0.5 wt% oxide (EDX measures O).\n- Furnaces are numbered 1 and 2; heat() says which one ran the job. env_log also lists reagent lots.\nThis project's samples are characterised by measurement; literature values for similarly named compounds do not apply.","compounds":{"C1":{"formula":"VTe2","prototype":"CdI2","space_group":"P-3m1 (164)","dopants":["Co","Zn"],"molar_mass":306.14},"C2":{"formula":"Ni3SbTe2","prototype":"Fe3GeTe2","space_group":"P6_3/mmc (194)","dopants":["Co","Ti"],"molar_mass":553.04},"C3":{"formula":"Fe3InTe2","prototype":"Fe3GeTe2","space_group":"P6_3/mmc (194)","dopants":["Co","Z